---
type Props = { city?: string };
const { city = "your city" } = Astro.props;
---

<h2>What a restoration job in {city} usually looks like</h2>
<p>
  After you call, this is what a restoration job typically looks like. Times
  vary. Mold can start in 24 to 48 hours if wet material sits.
</p>
<ol class="steps">
  <li>
    <strong>Talk and inspect.</strong> They ask what happened, where the water
    went, and whether you have insurance. On site they look for hidden wet spots
    in walls, pad, and under cabinets.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Pull standing water.</strong> Pumps and extractors take out what you
    can see so it does not keep feeding the floor and drywall.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Dry the structure.</strong> Air movers and dehumidifiers run for
    days, not hours. They should measure moisture, not just “it looks dry.”
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Clean what can be saved.</strong> Clean water and dirty water are
    different jobs. Sewage needs more than a fan.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Rebuild if needed.</strong> Pad, drywall, trim, and sometimes
    flooring come out. That part is often a separate insurance line from the
    dry-out.
  </li>
</ol>
<p>
  Ask the shop to show you moisture readings and photos. That is what insurance
  wants, and it is how you know the job is done.
</p>
